  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-atom-desktop-bnpl-container (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a bootstrap that downloads a platform-specific binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a DNS-TXT chunked fallback via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" or cmd.exe /c start /b. A /tmp/.analytics_state file throttles repeat downloads. The package's stated purpose (a \"container wrapper\") is unrelated to this behaviour.",
